cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "photon-transport-toolkit: Monte Carlo photon transport in turbid media, with phase- and polarization-resolved extensions"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Noureddin
    family-names: Sedki
    affiliation: "Berlin, Germany"
version: 1.7.0
date-released: "2026-08-12"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A weighted-photon Monte Carlo model of light transport in scattering and
  absorbing media, implemented from first principles following the MCML
  formulation and validated against analytically known limiting cases and an
  independent MATLAB/Octave re-derivation. Extended to arbitrarily layered
  media, to phase-resolved (coherent-field) transport producing speckle, and
  to polarization-resolved transport carrying a Jones vector and its optical
  path length together, with Rayleigh or Mie scattering. An optional
  JAX-batched backend covers Rayleigh scattering at large photon counts
  (recommended above roughly 150,000 photons on CPU, per a measured
  benchmark documented alongside a design fix that recovered it from an
  initial four-times-slower result). The grating spectrometer model
  originally distributed here now lives in the separate repository
  grating-spectrometer-model.
keywords:
  - optics
  - photonics
  - Monte Carlo
  - light scattering
  - turbid media
  - spectroscopy
  - biomedical optics
  - polarization
  - Mie scattering
  - speckle
